        "comments": "The assembly daSenVisc1.hap1.2 is based on 64x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome appears to represent an extremely degraded tetraploid. To the extent that the HiC no longer indicates the homeologous chromosomes. However, the sub genomes can still be identified by the background HiC signal.",
